    "source": "Change the weather over the table when the story calls for it (a storm rolls in, the fog lifts). The server rolls weather on its own at each dawn and on long journeys; call this only to overrule it. Rain and fog cut what anyone sees and give disadvantage on Perception by sight; a gale gives disadvantage on ranged attacks past 30 feet; frigid or hot air is a hazard on a long march; the board's light follows the sky outdoors.",
